speechtext:
-because they did not have the power; but when Lincoln came to find a medium of exchange to put his army on
a paying basis, to meet his obligations and to get a medium of exchange that would serve the United States government in the place of gold, of which they had none and which was withheld from them at that time, he used a national currency system. Of course they did not win the war with currency; they won it with fighting men and guns, but they used that national currency to put those men and guns to work in the service of that nation.
[Mr. McGeer.}
